      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Local Factors Affecting Utah Pricing"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice Assessment: In high-elevation or heavy snowfall areas like Park City, prices can skew higher ($150 to $600 ) because inspectors must carefully evaluate hidden freeze-thaw stresses and snow-load damage."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Home Size and Complexity: A standard 2,000 sq. ft. home stays near the lower end. Homes with multiple stories, steep pitches, or highly complex rooflines add hazardous structural challenges, which increase the labor time or necessitate drone use."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Roof Certifications: If you are buying or selling a home and need a formal \"Roof Certification\" (guaranteeing the roof's lifespan for 2\u20135 years), it usually costs an additional $75 to $200 on top of the inspection baseline."
          }
        ]
      },
